{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_supervision", "label": "Supervision", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A supervisor one level up has the wider view: it knows whether the crashed actor is replaceable, holds critical state, or should give up entirely.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "label": "Die vier Direktiven (Restart / Resume / Stop / Escalate)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Restart is the default; Resume keeps state and skips the failing message, which is wrong when the state itself caused the throw.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_oneforonestrategy", "label": "OneForOneStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The default scope: children are usually independent, so a crashing session must not touch the others.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_allforonestrategy", "label": "AllForOneStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Only for children that share state or coordinate tightly, such as a producer-consumer pair on an internal channel.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_decideby", "label": "decideBy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_restart_semantics", "label": "Restart-Semantik", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "preRestart, discard, rebuild, postRestart, mailbox retained, failing message dropped \u2014 restart deliberately preserves no in-memory state, because let-it-crash trusts the recovery path more than a per-message guard.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_stopchildrenonrestart", "label": "stopChildrenOnRestart()", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Children are stopped because postRestart re-runs preStart, and an actor spawning a named child there would hit 'Child name is not unique' on the first restart; opting out needs an idempotent preStart that adopts the surviving child from the cell, and it is its own hook because the teardown must be awaited.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_restart_limits", "label": "maxRetries + withinTimeRangeMs", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "What breaks infinite restart loops; the parent-side counter includes the triggering failure, so maxRetries 10 tolerates eleven restarts before the twelfth failure stops the child.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_builtin_strategies", "label": "defaultStrategy / stoppingStrategy / escalatingStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_escalation_chain", "label": "Die Eskalations-Kette", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Uncaught errors only happen when every level escalates to the root; stops are a normal expected outcome, escalation-to-root is the 'we do not know what to do' signal.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_let_it_crash", "label": "Let it crash", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Inherited from Erlang: handling every error inline at the call site is brittle compared with a supervisor that can choose restart, resume, stop or escalate per error class.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_typed_wrapper_counting", "label": "Behaviors.supervise z\u00e4hlt anders", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "It reads maxRetries literally and escalates past the limit instead of stopping, because the typed wrapper sits inside the failing actor \u2014 stopping there would discard the failure with nobody above learning of it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_supervision_async_escape_hazard", "label": "Losgel\u00f6ste Callbacks umgehen die Supervision", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The supervisor only sees what onReceive throws or rejects with; raw setTimeout or escaped promise chains 